From: Chitkul Lakshya <chitkullakshya@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:40:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20replace=20Kokoro=20TTS=20with=20Pip?=
 =?UTF-8?q?er=20TTS=20=E2=80=94=20270=20MB=20RAM=20reduction?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces kokoro-micro (350 MB RAM, 1.7s load) with piper-rs (80 MB RAM,
85ms load) to meet the 250-300 MB idle RAM target.

Changes:
- Cargo.toml: replace kokoro-micro with piper-rs 0.2
- tts.rs: rewrite to use piper_rs::Piper instead of kokoro_micro::TtsEngine
  - Piper model: en_US-amy-medium (~63 MB, 22050 Hz, MOS 4.0-4.3)
  - Model auto-downloads from HuggingFace on first speak (one-time)
  - Also checks resources/piper/ for bundled models (production)
  - Cache stores (samples, sample_rate) — Piper uses 22050, not 24000
  - Speed: Piper length_scale = 1.0/speed (opposite of Kokoro)
  - All existing features preserved: speak_cached, tts:audio-started,
    barge-in, meeting mode, TTS volume control
- lib.rs: update TtsState to include sample_rate field
- ttsPlayer.ts: update voice list from Kokoro voices to Piper voice
  - af_sky → default (en_US-amy-medium)
  - provider type: "kokoro" → "piper"

RAM impact:
  Before: 578 MB idle (after first speak, Kokoro loaded)
  After:  293 MB idle (after first speak, Piper loaded)
  Savings: 285 MB (49% reduction)

Quality impact:
  MOS: 4.5 → 4.0-4.3 (imperceptible for short ack phrases)
  Load time: 1700ms → 85ms (95% faster)

New dependencies: piper-rs 0.2 (pulls in ort 2.0.0-rc.12, espeak-rs)
Removed dependencies: kokoro-micro 1.0

Tests: 93 Rust tests pass, 808 frontend modules build

